{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>Akh.</b> Joshua and Caleb went out, who did not take their portion by lot but by the word of HaShem." "<b>Akh by lot shall the land be divided.</b> [A masculine form applied to a feminine.] But before you divide the land into fifty-seven portions, they divided it by lot according to the names of the tribes of their fathers' fathers, for each head of a family. How so? They divided it into twelve districts corresponding to the twelve tribes, and wrote the names of the twelve districts corresponding to the twelve tribes, and wrote the names of the twelve districts on twelve slips, and placed them in one urn; and the names of the twelve tribes on twelve slips in one urn. And the official draws from the urn of districts and from the urn of tribes, and raises in one hand a slip of 'such-and-such a tribe' and in the other hand a slip of 'such-and-such a district.' Thus each tribe gains the district that comes up for it, and so for all of them. And according to the size of the tribe or the smallness of the tribe, they would expand or contract the boundary of a given tribe's district adjacent to another's, to give each one what is fitting for it, as it is written above: 'לרב תרבה נחלתו' etc. And if they divided the land first by lot into fifty-seven portions for fifty-seven heads of families, and afterward into twelve portions for twelve tribes, this one would find his portion in a tribe not his own, and that one his portion in a tribe not his own; but it is written: 'וירא את ישראל שוכן לשבטיו,' and it is written: 'איש מנחלת מטה אבתיו ידבקו בני ישראל.'" "<b>לשמות מטות אבתם.</b> Converts and slaves are excluded."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {1 "The bracketed editorial note '[a masculine form applied to a feminine]' addresses the masculine verb יחלק used where the feminine noun הארץ is the subject/object; rendered as a grammatical gloss as Chizkuni likely received it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:58.719225388Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}